--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Mutexes in an array whose size is symbolic: every lock is a store into one
array the solver keeps whole, so the array theory adds an Ackermann pair for
every two indices of every array term. Terms built as `c ? a : b` or
`a with [i := v]` no longer get pairs of their own -- their consistency
follows from a and b through the if/with constraints over the same index
set -- which here takes the pairs from 6805 to 4039 and the run from about
15 s to 3 s.

A known-answer test for that path, not a bug fix: SUCCESSFUL before and
after. See `array_theory_lock_array_race`, which must stay FAILED.
